vl, gtk: vmlab: the window's clipboard is on; full screen at the screen's size; the offered size in a file

The GTK window opened beside egl-headless (0002) had QEMU's clipboard sharing off, GTK's
default, so nothing copied on one side reached the other: it is on (0009 gives it pictures).

A guest that keeps the window's first size (VMLAB_WINDOW_FIXED_SIZE=first) is offered the
window's size again when the window goes to the whole screen and when it comes back: full
screen is the screen's own size, with no bands beside the picture.

VMLAB_WINDOW_SIZE_FILE names a file that gets the size last offered to such a guest, as WxH.
Windows, shown a size it has not seen before while it starts, sometimes settles on 1024x768
and keeps that for the size; a helper outside reads the file and sets the mode in the guest
(win-venus.sh).

The picture's surface (0007) comes off the window at the full screen toggle and goes back
when GTK has drawn the window at its new size. A picture that covers the window whole, as in
full screen, leaves the compositor nothing of the window to draw, so mutter sends the window
no frame callback; GTK 3 waits for one before it draws, and never drew the window at the size
it got when leaving full screen (the window stayed over the whole screen with no title bar).

